        <div class="card" style="margin-top:16px">
          <h3><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"></path><path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"></path></svg>英语精读 · CET6 真题风格文章</h3>
          <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)">六级真题风格 · 更长更难的长难句 + 学术话题词汇 / 译文 / 精析 / 我的笔记 · 每天精读1篇</p>
          <div id="cet6ReadingContainer"><div style="margin-bottom:12px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px"><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--hint)">第 6 篇 / 共 6 篇 · 六级真题风格 · 点"换一篇"切换</span><button class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" onclick="nextCet6Reading()">换一篇</button></div><div class="card" style="margin-bottom:16px"><h3>Passage 6 · 城市化与生活质量（难度 ★★★☆）</h3><h4>原文</h4><p style="line-height:2.0;color:var(--text);font-size:16px">Urbanization has long been associated with economic progress, yet its impact on quality of life is far from straightforward. Megacities attract talent and capital, fostering innovation and cultural vitality; simultaneously, they confront overcrowding, soaring housing costs, and environmental strain. Recent studies suggest that well-designed public spaces and efficient transit systems can significantly mitigate these pressures, enhancing residents' well-being without sacrificing urban dynamism. The future of cities thus hinges less on their size than on the wisdom of their planning.</p><h4>重点词汇</h4><div style="margin-bottom:6px"><span class="tag tag-teal" style="margin:2px 4px 2px 0;display:inline-block">urbanization n.城市化</span><span class="tag tag-teal" style="margin:2px 4px 2px 0;display:inline-block">vitality n.活力；生命力</span><span class="tag tag-teal" style="margin:2px 4px 2px 0;display:inline-block">mitigate v.缓解；减轻</span><span class="tag tag-teal" style="margin:2px 4px 2px 0;display:inline-block">well-being n.幸福感；福祉</span><span class="tag tag-teal" style="margin:2px 4px 2px 0;display:inline-block">dynamism n.活力；动态性</span></div><h4>中文译文</h4><p style="background:var(--bg);padding:14px;border-radius:8px;line-height:2.0;font-size:15px">城市化长期以来与经济发展相关联，但它对生活质量的影响远非简单明了。特大城市吸引人才与资本，激发创新与文化活力；与此同时，它们也面临拥挤、房价飙升和环境压力。近期研究表明，设计良好的公共空间与高效的交通系统能显著缓解这些压力，在提升居民福祉的同时不牺牲城市的活力。因此，城市的未来更多取决于规划智慧，而非规模大小。</p><h4>长难句精析</h4><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.9;font-size:15px">长难句：Recent studies suggest that well-designed public spaces and efficient transit systems can significantly mitigate these pressures, enhancing residents' well-being without sacrificing urban dynamism. 主干 studies suggest that...；enhancing... 为结果状语。</p><h4>思考题</h4><div style="padding:6px 0;border-top:1px dashed var(--border);font-size:14px"><strong style="color:var(--primary)">Q：</strong> 城市化对生活质量的真实影响？<br><strong style="color:var(--teal)">A：</strong> 利弊并存——促创新增活力，也带来拥挤房价压力；关键在规划智慧。</div><h4>我的笔记</h4><textarea id="c6n_5_Passage " placeholder="写下你的理解、生词、仿写句...（自动保存）" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.8" onblur="saveCet6NoteKey(&#39;5_Passage &#39;,this.value)"></textarea><button class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" style="margin-top:8px" onclick="saveCet6NoteKey(&#39;5_Passage &#39;,document.getElementById(&#39;c6n_5_Passage &#39;).value)">保存笔记</button><span style="font-size:12px;color:var(--teal);margin-left:10px" id="c6nSaved_5_Passage "></span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tab-pane" id="t-law">
